<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gough Whitlam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1916–2014</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gough Whitlam was the Labor prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> from 1972 to 1975. His government ended conscription and withdrew from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a>, recognised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>, formally ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-australia-policy">White Australia policy</a> and introduced universal health insurance and free university education. On 11 November 1975 he was dismissed by Governor-General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sir-john-kerr">Sir John Kerr</a> after the Senate blocked supply.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gough-whitlam.jpg" alt="Gough Whitlam" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Work of the Australian Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gough_Whitlam_at_the_Lodge_1974.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
